{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-016",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 16,
  "title": "Proverbs 16",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 16",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 16,
  "sortOrder": 20016,
  "verseCount": 33,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The preparations of the heart in man, and the answer of the tongue, is from the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes; but the LORD weigheth the spirits.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The LORD hath made all things for himself: yea, even the wicked for the day of evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD: though hand join in hand, he shall not be unpunished.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "By mercy and truth iniquity is purged: and by the fear of the LORD men depart from evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "When a man’s ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Better is a little with righteousness than great revenues without right.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "A man’s heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "A divine sentence is in the lips of the king: his mouth transgresseth not in judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "A just weight and balance are the LORD’s: all the weights of the bag are his work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "It is an abomination to kings to commit wickedness: for the throne is established by righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Righteous lips are the delight of kings; and they love him that speaketh right.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "The wrath of a king is as messengers of death: but a wise man will pacify it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "In the light of the king’s countenance is life; and his favour is as a cloud of the latter rain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "How much better is it to get wisdom than gold! and to get understanding rather to be chosen than silver!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The highway of the upright is to depart from evil: he that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Better it is to be of an humble spirit with the lowly, than to divide the spoil with the proud.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "He that handleth a matter wisely shall find good: and whoso trusteth in the LORD, happy is he.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Understanding is a wellspring of life unto him that hath it: but the instruction of fools is folly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The heart of the wise teacheth his mouth, and addeth learning to his lips.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Pleasant words are as an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "There is a way that seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He that laboureth laboureth for himself; for his mouth craveth it of him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "An ungodly man diggeth up evil: and in his lips there is as a burning fire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "A froward man soweth strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "A violent man enticeth his neighbour, and leadeth him into the way that is not good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "He shutteth his eyes to devise froward things: moving his lips he bringeth evil to pass.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "The hoary head is a crown of glory, if it be found in the way of righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "He that is slow to anger is better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh a city.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:16:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "The lot is cast into the lap; but the whole disposing thereof is of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 16:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:16:33"
      }
    }
  ],
